          "description": "The plane's tooltip and name (`<epic-send-buttons send-tip>`)."
        },
        {
          "key": "loading",
          "text": "Reading the run…",
          "description": "Before the run is read."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "epic-run-row",
      "name": "epic-run-row",
      "folder": "epic-run-row",
      "mainTag": "epic-run-row",
      "main": true,
      "page": true,
      "href": "epic-run-row.html",
      "topics": [
        "answering"
      ],
      "aka": [
        "run row",
        "command row",
        "review row",
        "name review"
      ],
      "description": "One row of a run page (epic `epic-engine` P23), drawn by `<epic-run>` in its table:  the command's own columns, then the answer.  The answer is the command's proposal, pre-filled in a box Owen types over;  a pick of the few alternatives the command offers, when it offers any, with the proposal first;  the row's tick box, with the command's own label (`Use for every project`);  and its details, folded under it.  Each change says so (`epic-run-answer`), and `<epic-run>` saves it:  typing half a second after he stops, a pick or a tick at once.  A row he answered differently from the proposal is orange, with a round button putting the proposal back.  A row the command has taken (acted on, epic `epic-engine` P25) has a quiet `taken` mark, its time in the tooltip;  changed after that, an orange note says so:  the command may pick the change up if it can.",
      "noun": "run row",
      "attributes": [
        {
          "name": "row",
          "kind": "json",
          "description": "The row, as the command wrote it (`RunRow`, the kit's `spell/server/runs/runs.types`):  `id`, `cells`, `value` (the proposal), `alternatives`, `tick`, `details`.  A property;  JSON in markup."
        },
        {
          "name": "columns",
          "kind": "json",
          "description": "The run's columns (`RunColumn[]`:  `key`, `label`), in order:  which `cells` to show, and their names."
        },
        {
          "name": "answer",
          "kind": "json",
          "description": "Owen's answer so far (`RunAnswer`:  `outcome`, `value`, `ticked`), as saved;  none:  the proposal, and the tick box as the command set it."
        },
        {
          "name": "answer-label",
          "kind": "string",
          "description": "The answer column's name (`Spanish`):  the box's name."
        },
        {
          "name": "taken",
          "kind": "string",
          "description": "When the command took the row (acted on it), ISO (`RunPage.taken`, P25);  none:  not taken yet.  An answer saved after it is `changed-after-taken`."
        }
      ],
      "slots": [],
      "events": [
        {
          "name": "epic-run-answer",
          "detail": "{ rowId: string, outcome: RunOutcome, value: string, ticked?: boolean, now: boolean }",
          "description": "Owen answered the row:  typed in the box (`now: false`, saved a moment later), picked an alternative or ticked the box (`now: true`).  `outcome` says which:  `accepted` (the proposal), `picked` (an alternative), `typed` (anything else)."
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
          "name": "base",
          "description": "Its cells, laid out on its table's columns."
        },
        {
          "name": "cell",
          "description": "One of the command's columns:  its value, as text."
        },
        {
          "name": "answer",
          "description": "The answer cell:  the box, the pick, the tick box, the details."
        },
        {
          "name": "box",
          "description": "The `<textarea>`:  one line of text that wraps and grows;  Enter adds no line."
        },
        {
          "name": "reset",
          "description": "The round button putting the proposal back, once the box holds something else."
        },
        {
          "name": "picks",
          "description": "The pick:  the proposal, then each alternative, as small pills;  the chosen one raised, as a segmented control's thumb."
        },
        {
          "name": "pick",
          "description": "One pill of the pick."
        },
        {
          "name": "tick",
          "description": "The tick box and its label."
        },
        {
          "name": "details",
          "description": "Its details, folded:  a line each."
        },
        {
          "name": "taken",
          "description": "The quiet `taken` mark beside the box:  a check and the word, its time the tooltip."
        },
        {
          "name": "changed-after-taken",
          "description": "The orange note under the box:  the answer changed after the command took the row."
        }
      ],
      "states": [
        {
          "name": "changed",
          "description": "The answer isn't the proposal:  orange."
        },
        {
          "name": "answered",
          "description": "Owen answered it (anything saved, the proposal included)."
        },
        {
          "name": "taken",
          "description": "The command took the row (acted on it)."
        },
        {
          "name": "changed-after-taken",
          "description": "Owen's answer is newer than the command's taking of it:  the orange note shows."
